It tests all the repo set (so bioconductor (*3), cran and r-forge) and
stops at the first positive hit.

> As I said this is a really small detail.
It is, but potentially annoying, especially if one package is present in
more than one repository (and with different version), which is the
case.
It will then stop at the first positive match and won't look further. So
potentially, it might be annoying, I'll try to fix this.

Good to hear that you like it !

Thanks for all,

Pierre

